# Local agent communication
.comms/
.codex/AGENTS.md
.codex/config.toml
.agent-comms/

# Session worktrees created INSIDE the checkout. Snapshot-on-send captures untracked
# files, so an un-ignored worktree puts an entire second copy of the repo into every
# review artifact — reviewers then see two of every file and cannot tell which is under
# review. Worktrees are ephemeral working state, never part of an artifact.
.claude/worktrees/

# Install OUTPUT, not source. `install.sh --scope=local` writes these from templates/ and
# docs/loopspec/fragments/; checking them in would duplicate the source and invite drift (an
# audit already caught the installed auto.md 298 bytes behind its template). They must stay on
# disk — the three-tier resolver deliberately prefers a project pin, and `prompt-version` hashes
# whichever copy actually resolves — but they are machine-local state, not repository content.
# Ignoring them also keeps them OUT of review artifacts: snapshot-on-send captures untracked
# files, so every un-ignored install copy is duplicated into every snapshot a reviewer reads.
.claude/commands/
.agents/
